<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB sells no wheat in twelfth tender.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB sells no wheat in twelfth tender.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) rejected all bids and sold no wheat in its twelfth tender, it said in a statement. Bids were submitted for only 2,000 tonnes of new crop wheat in one zone but none was sold at tender, AWB said. The AWB said highest failed bids in A$ a tonne were:</p>
<p>    Port Zone	 Grade			Bids</p>
<p>    Esperance	  AH			  198.00</p>
<p>Closing date for the next tender is December 16.</p>
<p>NOTE - AH: Australian Hard.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 973-1800</p>
